 2. 🦾 New AI models tout affordability 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Eniola Odetunde/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Cheaper, more powerful AI models could pave the way for top labs to safely slow development without going broke, Axios' Madison Mills writes. 

 Why it matters: OpenAI, Anthropic and other labs have said they want to slow the pace of development. But as long as frontier models require ever-larger spending, the pressure to keep racing may be too strong to resist. 🖼️ The big picture: The health of the entire U.S. economy now rests in part on the AI boom. Yet the companies at the center of the race are burning far more cash than they take in, and will for the foreseeable future.

 To enable a slowdown, in a financial sense, the companies have to find a way to build a value proposition to users that isn't solely rooted in the most mind-blowing intelligence imaginable. 🔬 Zoom in: This week brought a spate of new models. One thing they all have in common is that they're cheaper than ever, without forgoing top intelligence.

 OpenAI, Anthropic and SpaceX all emphasized the relatively low costs of their new models, as well as their ability to outperform some of their own top systems from only a few months ago. Keep reading ... Get Axios AI+ . 

 
 
