 3. ⚡ Scoop: $2B Gaza recovery plan 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Workers search the rubble of a Gaza City building that collapsed last week. It had been damaged by an Israeli strike earlier in the war. Photo: Dawoud Abu Alkas/Reuters President Trump's Board of Peace will unveil a six-month, $2.45 billion recovery plan for Gaza at a meeting of its members today, Axios' Barak Ravid reports from New York. 

 Why it matters: The 66-project proposal offers one of the most comprehensive roadmaps yet for what the early months of post-war reconstruction and governance in Gaza would look like. The plan includes money for temporary housing, rubble removal, hospital repairs, economic recovery and the deployment of a multinational security force, according to a copy obtained by Axios.

 The plan estimates physical damage in Gaza at $35.2 billion and says full recovery and reconstruction will require about $71.4 billion over the next decade. A Board of Peace official said that "the plan shows how to stand up a government from nothing, an economy from shambles and a territory from disaster." 🥊 Reality check: For the plan to work, the Board of Peace needs Israel and Hamas to cooperate.

 While Bibi's government agreed in principle to aspects of the plan that were previously discussed, Israel refused to start implementing it, mainly for domestic political reasons ahead of next month's elections. And while Hamas has agreed in principle to disarm, that pledge hasn't been tested. More on the plan . 

 
 
