 4. ⚖️ Poll: Americans say rule of law is declining 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Charles F. Kettering Foundation and Gallup. Chart: Noah Bressner/Axios Visuals A majority of Americans (56%) say the rule of law in the U.S. is weaker now than a decade ago, when Donald Trump was first elected president, Axios' Margaret Talev writes from a massive new survey of more than 23,000 U.S. adults. 

 78% of those responding to the survey by Gallup and the Charles F. Kettering Foundation for its Democracy for All Project say government officials must always follow laws and the Constitution. But just 28% trust that political leaders will be held accountable if they don't. Keep reading . 

 
 
