 5. 🚕 Uber&#x27;s robotaxi edge: Human drivers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Uber is betting billions on a driverless future, but the secret to making the economics work could be — surprise! — its vast army of human drivers, Axios' Joann Muller writes. 

 Why it matters: Uber believes a hybrid network of robots and people can keep its expensive autonomous vehicles busier, and therefore more profitable, than fleets made up entirely of robotaxis. 💡 How it works: In a hybrid network, AVs would handle the steady "base load" of everyday demand.

 Human drivers would provide extra capacity during rush hour, bad weather, concerts and other demand spikes. Keep reading ... Get Axios Future of Mobility . 

 
 
