 6. 🗳️ Trump amps up hunt for voter fraud 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Photo: Jim Watson/AFP via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Trump administration says Americans should prepare between now and Election Day for a wave of new arrests and prosecutions over alleged noncitizen voter fraud, Axios' Brittany Gibson writes. 

 Why it matters: The Trump administration is deploying hundreds of federal investigators and attorneys to pursue President Trump's long-running fixation — and test a broader Republican claim that tougher enforcement will uncover far more illegal voting. A Justice Department official told reporters yesterday that the "initiative is a tier one priority. It's a top priority for the attorney general and for the White House."

 Across the country, there are now 1,600 open cases of potential voter fraud and 160 people have been arrested, a Homeland Security Investigations official said. To support these investigations, Homeland Security staff have shifted work time from other priorities such as smuggling, trafficking and financial fraud. Reality check: Instances of mistaken registrations and cases of noncitizen voting are rare, but they've long been investigated by the federal government.

