 7. 🎧 Charted: Music&#x27;s new record 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Billboard . Chart: Noah Bressner/Axios Country sensation Ella Langley's "Choosin' Texas" is now the longest-running No. 1 song in the Billboard Hot 100's history after spending 23 weeks in the top spot, Axios' Sara Fischer and Neal Rothschild write. 

 It passed Mariah Carey's "All I Want for Christmas Is You," which accumulated 22 weeks at No. 1 across seven holiday seasons. Between the lines: More songs are staying on the charts for longer as streaming algorithms encourage repeat listens and vertical video platforms serve as extended marketing tools.

