 8. 🐧 1 fun thing: Penguin acupuncture 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: New England Aquarium New England Aquarium veterinarians are turning to acupuncture to help out their oldest penguin, Axios Boston's Mike Deehan writes. 

 Pip, a 29-year-old African penguin, has lived about twice as long as his species typically survives in the wild. Staff noticed Pip's limp and altered gait late last year, and feared arthritis-related conditions common in older penguins.

 After trying pain medication, vets added acupuncture and physical therapy from an outside specialist to Pip's routine. Share this story ... Get Axios Local : Newsletters in 43 cities. 

 
 
